  "id": "stereoscope",
  "term": "stereoscope",
  "definition": "A stereoscope is a device used to present two companion images separately to the two eyes so they can be fused into a single binocular percept. In this context, a hand-held mirror stereoscope enables cross-fusion, which can make local visual differences stand out during search tasks.",
